-- חוק שוויון ההזדמנויות בעבודה, התשמ"ח-1988 — sections 2, 3, 4 and 17:
-- that an employer does not discriminate between employees, among other
-- grounds by sex, personal status or parenthood, in their conditions of
-- work and their pay; that a provision on pregnancy, birth or nursing and a
-- better right given to a woman are not discrimination; that a right
-- connected with parenthood a mother has at her workplace is a father's
-- too, where his spouse works and did not take it or the child is in his
-- sole custody; and that the State is an employer like any other. The text
-- is laws/equal-opportunities-law.toml, pinned from the live page of ספר
-- החוקים הפתוח; the corpus holds no copy (MMS-601).
--
-- Why it is here: five documents apply §4(א) to the day-care supplement
-- ("ויחולו לגביה הוראות סעיף 4(א) לחוק האמור"), and the instruments that
-- give a mother a shorter week or a day-care supplement give a father less
-- or more than §4 does. Where an instrument gives less, the law governs (the
-- root's precedence, l4/lib/precedence.l4; convention
-- instruments.statute-floor).

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT parties

@desc An employee who is a father, as section 4(א) asks about his family.
DECLARE `a father's family under section 4` HAS
    `his spouse is an employee or self-employed`  IS A BOOLEAN @desc section 4(א)(1)
    `his spouse took the right herself`           IS A BOOLEAN @desc she was absent from her work by her own entitlement to it (section 4(ב)(1)-(2)), or used it (4(ב)(3)-(4))
    `the child is in his sole custody`            IS A BOOLEAN @desc section 4(א)(2): "בהחזקתו הבלעדית"

`a father whose spouse works and does not take the right` MEANS
    `a father's family under section 4` WITH
        `his spouse is an employee or self-employed` IS TRUE
        `his spouse took the right herself`          IS FALSE
        `the child is in his sole custody`           IS FALSE

`a father whose spouse takes the right herself` MEANS
    `a father's family under section 4` WITH
        `his spouse is an employee or self-employed` IS TRUE
        `his spouse took the right herself`          IS TRUE
        `the child is in his sole custody`           IS FALSE

`a father whose spouse does not work` MEANS
    `a father's family under section 4` WITH
        `his spouse is an employee or self-employed` IS FALSE
        `his spouse took the right herself`          IS FALSE
        `the child is in his sole custody`           IS FALSE

`a father with the child in his sole custody` MEANS
    `a father's family under section 4` WITH
        `his spouse is an employee or self-employed` IS FALSE
        `his spouse took the right herself`          IS FALSE
        `the child is in his sole custody`           IS TRUE

§ `חוק שוויון ההזדמנויות בעבודה — איסור הפליה וזכויות הורה`

§§ `2`

-- (א): an employer does not discriminate between his employees, or between
-- job seekers, for their sex, sexual orientation, personal status (single,
-- married, divorced or widowed — §1), pregnancy, fertility or IVF
-- treatment, being parents, age, race, religion, nationality, country of
-- origin, place of residence, views, party, or reserve duty (theirs, their
-- spouses' or the other parent's), in any of: (1) hiring; (2) conditions of
-- work; (3) promotion; (4) training; (5) dismissal or severance pay; (6)
-- benefits and payments on retirement. (א1): an employer in fact does not
-- discriminate between a manpower contractor's workers he employs, nor ask
-- the contractor to. (ב): setting conditions that are not relevant counts
-- as discrimination. (ג): a distinction the character or nature of the job
-- or post requires is not.
@desc A ground section 2(א) names.
DECLARE `ground section 2 names` IS ONE OF
    `the employee's sex`
    `the employee's sexual orientation`
    `the employee's personal status`
    `the employee's pregnancy`
    `the employee's fertility or IVF treatment`
    `the employee's being a parent`
    `the employee's age`
    `the employee's race, religion, nationality or country of origin`
    `the employee's place of residence`
    `the employee's views or party`
    `the employee's or a spouse's reserve duty`

@desc A matter section 2(א)(1)-(6) names.
DECLARE `matter section 2 names` IS ONE OF
    `hiring`
    `conditions of work`
    `promotion at work`
    `vocational training`
    `dismissal or severance pay`
    `benefits and payments on retirement`

@desc What the Equal Opportunities Law forbids an employer.
DECLARE `Equal Opportunities Law act` IS ONE OF
    `discriminate between employees or job seekers` HAS
        `on the ground of` IS A `ground section 2 names`
        `in the matter of` IS A `matter section 2 names`

@ref law:2
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `Equal Opportunities Law act`
DECIDE `no discrimination under section 2` IS
    PARTY `the employer`
    SHANT `discriminate between employees or job seekers` g m
    LEST  BREACH BY `the employer` BECAUSE "Equal Opportunities Law, section 2: an employer does not discriminate between employees on a ground it names"

-- Whether a distinction an instrument makes is the discrimination (א)
-- forbids: one on a ground it names, in a matter it names, that the job
-- does not require (ג), and that §3 does not keep.
@ref law:2
GIVEN `a distinction on a ground section 2 names, in a matter it names` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the character or nature of the job requires it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc section 2(ג)
      `section 3 keeps it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `discrimination under section 2` `a distinction on a ground section 2 names, in a matter it names` `the character or nature of the job requires it` `section 3 keeps it` IF
        `a distinction on a ground section 2 names, in a matter it names`
    AND NOT `the character or nature of the job requires it`
    AND NOT `section 3 keeps it`

`setting irrelevant conditions counts as discrimination under section 2(ב)` MEANS TRUE
`section 2(א1) binds an employer in fact towards a manpower contractor's workers` MEANS TRUE

#ASSERT `discrimination under section 2` TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `discrimination under section 2` TRUE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `discrimination under section 2` TRUE FALSE TRUE

§§ `3`

-- (א): a provision of an enactment, a collective agreement or a contract
-- of employment on pregnancy, keeping a pregnancy, birth, nursing or
-- fertility is not discrimination. (ב): the law takes from a woman no
-- better right an enactment, a collective agreement or a contract of
-- employment gives her, and such a right is not discrimination.
@ref law:3
GIVEN `a provision on pregnancy, its keeping, birth, nursing or fertility` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a better right given to a woman by an enactment, a collective agreement or a contract` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 3 keeps it from being discrimination` `a provision on pregnancy, its keeping, birth, nursing or fertility` `a better right given to a woman by an enactment, a collective agreement or a contract` IF
        `a provision on pregnancy, its keeping, birth, nursing or fertility`
    OR  `a better right given to a woman by an enactment, a collective agreement or a contract`

#ASSERT `section 3 keeps it from being discrimination` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `section 3 keeps it from being discrimination` FALSE FALSE

§§ `4`

-- (ב): a "right connected with parenthood" is one of four, and no other:
-- (1) absence from work for the child's illness; (2) a shortened working
-- day for being the mother of a child; (3) the use of a day-care centre
-- the employer provides for the employees' children; (4) the employer's
-- share in the cost of keeping the child in day care.
@desc A right connected with parenthood, as section 4(ב) lists them.
DECLARE `right connected with parenthood` IS ONE OF
    `absence from work for the child's illness`
    `a shortened working day for being the mother of a child`
    `the use of a day-care centre the employer provides`
    `the employer's share in the cost of keeping the child in day care`

@ref law:4
GIVEN r IS A `right connected with parenthood`
GIVETH A STRING
DECIDE `the words of section 4(ב) for` r IS
    CONSIDER r
    WHEN `absence from work for the child's illness` THEN "(1) היעדרות מעבודה בשל מחלת הילד"
    WHEN `a shortened working day for being the mother of a child` THEN "(2) יום עבודה מקוצר בשל היות העובדת אם לילד"
    WHEN `the use of a day-care centre the employer provides` THEN "(3) זכות להשתמש בשירותי מעון שהמעסיק מעמיד לרשות ילדי העובדים"
    WHEN `the employer's share in the cost of keeping the child in day care` THEN "(4) השתתפות המעסיק בעלות החזקתו של הילד במעון"

-- (א): where a female employee has such a right by the conditions of work
-- customary at her workplace, a male employee at a workplace where those
-- conditions are customary has it too, if either (1) his spouse is an
-- employee or self-employed and was not absent, or did not use the right,
-- by her own entitlement to it; or (2) the child is in his sole custody.
-- The father's right is the mother's right as the workplace gives it: the
-- same conditions of age, position and amount bind him; nothing else does.
@ref law:4
GIVEN f IS A `a father's family under section 4`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 4(א)(1) holds for` f IF
        f's `his spouse is an employee or self-employed`
    AND NOT f's `his spouse took the right herself`

GIVEN f IS A `a father's family under section 4`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 4(א)(2) holds for` f IF
    f's `the child is in his sole custody`

GIVEN `a mother at his workplace has the right` IS A BOOLEAN @desc by the conditions of work customary there, on the same conditions of age, position and the rest that the father meets
      f IS A `a father's family under section 4`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 4 gives the father the right` `a mother at his workplace has the right` f IF
        `a mother at his workplace has the right`
    AND (    `section 4(א)(1) holds for` f
         OR  `section 4(א)(2) holds for` f)

#ASSERT `section 4 gives the father the right` TRUE `a father whose spouse works and does not take the right`
#ASSERT NOT `section 4 gives the father the right` TRUE `a father whose spouse takes the right herself`
#ASSERT NOT `section 4 gives the father the right` TRUE `a father whose spouse does not work`
#ASSERT `section 4 gives the father the right` TRUE `a father with the child in his sole custody`
#ASSERT NOT `section 4 gives the father the right` FALSE `a father whose spouse works and does not take the right`
#ASSERT `the words of section 4(ב) for` `the employer's share in the cost of keeping the child in day care` EQUALS "(4) השתתפות המעסיק בעלות החזקתו של הילד במעון"

§§ `17`

-- For this law, the State as an employer is like any other employer: it
-- binds the State, and so the Ministry of Education towards the teachers
-- it employs.
@ref law:17
`the Equal Opportunities Law binds the State as an employer` MEANS TRUE
